    "best_measured_config": "native_cuda single owner, active/batch=512/512, reused transport, compiled + projection, pipeline_slots=1: 58,468 sim/s mean over two windows (58,873 / 58,062), CPU 17.1-17.3 us/simulation.",
    "tier_ranking": "128/128 43,822 < 256/256 54,229 (52,434-56,443 over three windows) < 512/512 58,468 (58,062-58,873). The 256 and 512 samples do not overlap, so 512 is the best measured point; the 07 claim that they were indistinguishable came from wrong inputs and is withdrawn.",
    "buffer_reuse": "reused 54,229 sim/s (mean) vs packed 40,403 sim/s at 256/256 (+34% on means, +40% on the single paired windows), CPU 25.0 -> 17.8-19.2 us/simulation.",
    "cpu_tier": "native CPU 8x4 eager 16,433 sim/s / 469.5 us per simulation; compiled 14,423 sim/s / 533.0 us (-12% throughput, +13.5% CPU per simulation) -> keep eager on CPU.",
    "dual_slot": "256/128 slots=1 49,063 vs slots=2 47,119 sim/s (two windows each) -> no repeatable gain; overlap is real (D2H wait 0.29 -> 0.07 s, peak in-flight 256 vs 128 rows). Keep pipeline_slots=1.",
